Renaming a Fork does not remove these conditions. Separately licensed
third-party components retain their own terms; this License does not purport
to relicense them.

4. Activities requiring a separate agreement

A separate agreement with the Copyright Holder is required to:

(a) sell copies of the Program or a Fork;
(b) license a derivative version of the Program for a fee; or
(c) provide paid cloud access to the Program or a Fork.

Paid cloud access means charging others for hosted access to the Program or
Fork itself or its functionality. These restrictions do not prohibit using
Projector in your own commercial work or selling your independent work
products merely because Projector was used to create them.

You may charge for installation, support and commissioned modification,
provided that the Program or Fork itself is supplied free of charge. These
service fees do not authorize charging for copies, derivative licenses or
cloud access described above. When a Program or Fork is distributed, the
source, notice and same-license conditions in Section 3 still apply.

5. Independent extensions and other products

Independent plugins, harness adapters and integrations that do not include
